<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1976</h1><p class="ref-lede">1976 in world history: 14 events, 2 births, 14 deaths, 1 work, 1 state founded and 4 that came to an end. 207 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1972">1972</a><a href="/years/1973">1973</a><a href="/years/1974">1974</a><a href="/years/1975">1975</a><a href="/years/1976" aria-current="page">1976</a><a href="/years/1977">1977</a><a href="/years/1978">1978</a><a href="/years/1979">1979</a><a href="/years/1980">1980</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-21">21 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Concorde begins commercial supersonic service</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British Airways flew Concorde from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> and Air <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a> via <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dakar-senegal">Dakar</a>. Flying at twice the speed of sound, Concorde served passengers until 2003.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-janeiro">Rio de Janeiro</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-24">24 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Military coup overthrows Isabel Perón in Argentina</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A junta led by General Jorge Videla took power and began the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dirty-war">Dirty War</a>'. Thousands of people, estimated at up to 30,000, were 'disappeared' before military rule ended in 1983.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-1">1 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Jobs, Wozniak and Wayne found Apple Computer</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Steve Jobs, Steve Wozniak and Ronald Wayne signed the partnership that created Apple Computer in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>. Its first product was the hand-built Apple I; Wayne sold his share within days.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-16">16 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Police fire on students in Soweto</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Police shot at schoolchildren marching against compulsory <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikaans">Afrikaans</a> teaching, killing 13-year-old Hector Pieterson among others. The uprising spread, and hundreds died in the months that followed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-20">20 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Viking 1 makes the first successful landing on Mars</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">NASA's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> 1 lander touched down on Chryse Planitia and sent back the first photographs from the Martian surface. It operated for more than six years.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/soweto-uprising" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soweto-uprising.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/soweto-uprising">Soweto uprising</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soweto uprising began on 16 June 1976, when thousands of Black schoolchildren in Soweto, near Johannesburg, marched against the compulsory use of Afrikaans as a language of instruction.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/loyada-hostage-crisis">Loyada hostage crisis</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Loyada hostage crisis took place in February 1976, when militants of the Front for the Liberation of the Somali Coast seized a school bus carrying children of French military personnel in Djibouti and drove it to Loyada, on the border with Somalia.</p></div></li></ol></section>
